//! APG equipment records — full corpus ingest (SD-24 Epic 6 criteria
//! 6.2/6.3/6.4). Generated from the real PCGen corpus files
//! `apg_equip_general.lst` (93 records), `apg_equip_arms_armor.lst` (75
//! records), and `apg_equip_magic_items.lst` (170 records) — 338 total,
//! every real, active (non-`.MOD`, non-comment, non-`SOURCELONG`-header)
//! record across all three files. Not hand-authored; generated by a
//! one-off ingestion script against
//! `~/workspace/repos/pcgen/data/pathfinder/paizo/roleplaying_game/advanced_players_guide/`
//! (reachable from this environment) — do not hand-edit, regenerate if
//! the corpus changes. See `equipment_tables.rs`'s module doc comment for
//! the full field-sourcing methodology (`COST:`, `WT:`, `DESC:` tokens;
//! `OUTPUTNAME:` for the display `name`; the corpus's own `KEY:` token or
//! else the raw sortkey for `key`).
//!
//! **Correction to the SD-24 criterion 6.1 audit's documented count**:
//! the coverage matrix recorded 341 real APG equipment records
//! (94 + 76 + 171). Each of the three source files carries exactly one
//! `SOURCELONG:...` header line that is not itself an equipment record
//! but is not a `#`-comment or blank line either, so the audit's
//! `grep -vE '^\s*#|^\s*$'`-based count double-counted it as a record in
//! every one of the three files. The real count is 338 (93 + 75 + 170).
//! See this cycle's `## DISCOVERED` entry (`epic-6-audit-correction`).
//!
//! **`description` is `None` for every one of these 338 records.** Direct
//! inspection of all three corpus files (word-boundary-anchored,
//! tab-preceded `DESC:` token search) finds zero equipment records with a
//! description token anywhere in APG's equipment corpus — PCGen equipment
//! records generally do not carry prose descriptions the way spell
//! records do (equipment flavor text lives in the printed book's prose,
//! not the LST data). This is a genuine corpus limitation, not a parsing
//! gap; criterion 6.4 cannot reach 100% description coverage for
//! equipment from this corpus alone. See `risks-and-open-questions.md`
//! and this cycle's receipt.
//!
//! **`weight` is `None` for 19 of 338 records** (`WT:` token absent from
//! the corpus line) — a real, small, honest gap, not a parsing defect.

